.TH SETUP\-REPO 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
setup\-repo \- initialize KryX Linux kpm and gports repositories and keyring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup\-repo
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup\-repo
creates the standard KryX Linux repository configuration under
.I /
or an alternative target root
.RB ( \-\-root ):
.IR /etc/kpm.ini ,
.IR /etc/gports/sources.list ,
.IR /etc/gports/sources.list.d/ ,
.IR /etc/kpm/keys.d/ ,
.IR /etc/pkgadd.conf ,
and
.IR /var/lib/pkg/db .
It then synchronizes the remote binary repository index via
.B kpm sync
(unless
.B \-\-no\-sync
is specified).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-root \fIdir\fR
Target root directory (default:
.IR / ).
.TP
.B \-\-repo \fIowner/repo\fR
Binary GitHub repository slug (default:
.BR kryx-linux/ports ).
.TP
.B \-\-tag \fItag\fR
Binary release tag (default:
.BR rolling\-x86_64 ).
.TP
.B \-\-arch \fIarch\fR
Target architecture (default:
.BR x86_64 ).
.TP
.B \-\-index\-url \fIurl\fR
Explicit
.I index.json
URL overriding
.B \-\-repo
and
.BR \-\-tag .
.TP
.B \-\-ports\-dir \fIdir\fR
Local ports root path inside target root (default:
.IR /usr/ports ).
.TP
.B \-\-key \fIfile|url\fR
Trust an Ed25519 release signing public key in
.IR keys.d .
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Set
.B verify_signature = true
in generated
.IR kpm.ini .
.TP
.B \-\-sync\-ports
Also synchronize local ports via
.B gports \-u
if installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sync
Write configuration files without performing network I/O.
.TP
.B \-\-kpm\-bin \fIpath\fR
Explicit path to the static
.B kpm
binary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
setup\-repo
setup\-repo \-\-root /mnt \-\-key https://example.org/kryx.pub \-\-verify
setup\-repo \-\-root /mnt \-\-no\-sync
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setup (8),
.BR setup\-kryx (8),
.BR setup\-chroot (8),
.BR kpm (8),
